# Compatibility baseline: Chrome 49+ (unified baseline for desktop + mobile, incl. Android WebView / low-end Android devices)
# Compatibility is guaranteed by this file's explicit lower bound + Babel transpilation + core-js polyfills, independent of the Node version on the build machine.
# Note: do not use `not dead` — it would drop legacy WebView/Safari versions that are no longer updated from the target set.
# Vue 3 relies on Proxy (not polyfillable), which is only supported from Chrome 49 onward, so the baseline must not go below 49.
#
# Semantics: `chrome >= 49` is a range match (matches all released Chrome versions >= 49).
# @vitejs/plugin-legacy generates the legacy bundle (ES5 + core-js polyfills) based on the lowest common feature set
# of these targets — the oldest version (49) determines the transpilation and polyfill set. Legacy devices run the
# legacy bundle, while modern devices run the modern bundle built with Vite's default build.target
# ('baseline-widely-available'); the two never interfere with each other.
chrome >= 49
